From: Xiaomi BE18000 OpenWrt port
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: support per-radio MLO link info via NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS

On single-wiphy multi-radio devices running 802.11be MLO (e.g. ap-mld0
spanning radio0/radio1/radio2):
1. NL80211_CMD_GET_INTERFACE puts per-link frequency, center_freq1/2,
   channel_width, txpower, and link MAC inside NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS
   rather than top-level attributes.
2. NL80211_ATTR_VIF_RADIO_MASK has multiple bits set (e.g. 0x7); the
   loop in nl80211_get_mode_cb() previously overwrote radio_idx to the
   highest set bit, causing hostapd queries to read the wrong radio's
   config file.
3. Querying a UCI radio section (radio0/radio1/radio2) discarded its
   UCI `option radio` index when resolving the netdev and link attributes.

Resolve the UCI `option radio` index when given a radio section name,
filter nl80211_phy2ifname() candidates by VIF_RADIO_MASK, and select the
matching NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS entry for frequency, center_freq1/2,
txpower, channel width (htmode), and link BSSID.

--- a/iwinfo_nl80211.c
+++ b/iwinfo_nl80211.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 struct nl80211_if_data {
 	int mode;
 	int radio_idx;
+	uint32_t radio_mask;
 };
 
